skyrt changes to XenonRecomp (base: hedge-dev/XenonRecomp ddd128bcca99fe8bfbb99bea583c972351fa6ace).

- Implements instructions Skyrim uses that upstream lacks: addc, addme,
  subfze, eqv, lhbrx, load/store-with-update forms (lhzu, lhau, lfsu, lfdu,
  sthu, stfsu, stfdu, lbzux, lhzux, lwzux, lfsux, lfdux, stbux, sthux, stfsux,
  stdux), dcbst, frsqrte, lvehx, vsel128, vandc, vnor/vnor128, vslh, vsrh,
  vspltish, vctuxs, vpkswss128, vpkuwum, vsubuws, vsubshs, vadduhs, vaddsws,
  vslo/vslo128, bdzf, bdnzt.
- bdnzf honours its BI operand instead of assuming cr.eq.
- blrl calls through LR (upstream emits a debug trap); vupkd3d128 handles
  float16_2 and float16_4 and vpkd3d128 handles float16_2 (pack mode 1), using
  Xenia's Xenos half-float rules via helpers in cpp/ppc_context.h.
- vpkd3d128 float16_4 accepts pack mode 3 (same merge as mode 2 for shifts
  0-2, per Xenia).
- Switch tables without an `r` key dispatch on the target address in CTR
  (`cargo xtask switches` emits these), so the index register may be dead by
  the bctr.
- The switch table file may also carry [[function]] address/size entries.
- bdz/bdnz (upstream) and the new CTR-branch forms emit a call followed by a
  return for targets outside the function instead of an undeclared label.
- Every guest memory access the recompiler emits inline (vector loads and
  stores, lwarx/ldarx/stwcx./stdcx., dcbz/dcbzl, setjmp/longjmp) goes through
  PPC_EA(ea) instead of `base + ea`, like the PPC_LOAD/PPC_STORE macros, so
  ppc_context.h can fold the aliased physical views onto one mapping.
  ppc_config.h defines PPC_SKYRT_EA to mark output from this recompiler.
- The inline stores (dcbz/dcbzl, stvx/stvx128, stwcx./stdcx.) compute their
  address into `ea` and follow the store with PPC_MARK_WRITTEN(ea, size), which
  ppc_context.h uses to track pages written for the renderer (the PPC_STORE
  macros mark too). ppc_config.h defines PPC_SKYRT_DIRTY for this.

Applied by `cargo xtask setup-xenonrecomp`.

